cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
title: Wright–Fisher State‑Space Model for Bayesian Deconvolution and Early Detection of SARS‑CoV‑2 Lineages in Wastewater
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
repository-code: https://github.com/example/wf-wastewater
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: Wastewater Genomics Methods Consortium
abstract: >
  A deterministic, config‑driven, non‑package Python repository implementing a Wright–Fisher
  state‑space prior for lineage dynamics, empirical‑Bayes Beta–Binomial observation models for SNV counts,
  constrained deconvolution, particle filtering with MAP smoothing, sequential e‑value and Shiryaev–Roberts
  detection, and full diagnostics/validation for wastewater SARS‑CoV‑2 lineage surveillance.
keywords:
  - wastewater epidemiology
  - SARS-CoV-2
  - Wright–Fisher
  - state-space models
  - particle filtering
  - empirical Bayes
  - deconvolution
  - sequential detection
